@startuml uc-customer-tracking
' Use case — Customer tracking, history and receipts
' Recreated from UC-03_customer_tracking.puml by Supuni (Role 7); original kept as ../UC-03_customer_tracking-original.*
' Fixes per docs/architecture.md v1.2 §6.3 and parcel-service design (Role 3): receipt is available for any own parcel
' (not only DELIVERED); another customer's parcel returns 404 (not 403); SMS only on 3 statuses and goes to the recipient
' Layout: "Base <.. Extension" keeps the base use case next to the actor; the arrow still points at the base.
!include _style.iuml
left to right direction
title SwiftDrop – Customer tracking, history and receipts

actor "Customer" as Customer
actor "Guest\n(not logged in)" as Guest

rectangle "SwiftDrop" {
  usecase "Receive status\nnotifications" as C15
  usecase "View my deliveries\n(delivery history)" as C10
  usecase "View parcel details" as C11
  usecase "View status history\n(who, when, note, proof)" as C11a
  usecase "Download receipt (PDF)" as C13
  usecase "Track parcel by\ntracking number (public)" as C14
  usecase "Follow live updates\n(Server-Sent Events)" as C12
}

actor "Email / SMS\ngateway" as Notify <<system>>
actor "Recipient\n(no account)" as Recipient

Customer -- C15
Customer -- C10
Customer -- C11
Customer -- C14
Guest -- C14
C11 ..> C11a : <<include>>
C11 <.. C13 : <<extend>>
C14 <.. C12 : <<extend>>\n[not DELIVERED or FAILED]
C15 -- Notify
Recipient -- C15
' layout only: keep the gateway in a column right of the boundary; the Recipient is a person, so it sits with the people on the left
C11a -[hidden]- Notify

legend bottom right
  Only the owner, a Dispatcher or an Admin sees a parcel; anyone else gets 404,
  so parcel IDs cannot be probed. Customer booking: email to the customer on every
  change; SMS to the recipient on OUT_FOR_DELIVERY, DELIVERED and FAILED.
endlegend
@enduml
